  :body "The cascade for instance 5. It has NO missing meet, and the correction is worth recording: an earlier run of meets.clj reported three, all of them comparable pairs \u2014 one pattern below the other \u2014 which the strict reading of descendants dropped from their own common part. In containment terms if A contains B then A meet B = B, which is in the cascade. Recomputed with reflexive descendants, matching CascadeOrder.Below in the PROOF-2a Lean module (a = b OR Reach r a b): 19 overlapping pairs, 19 with a greatest common descendant. Across all five cascades the strict reading showed five missing meets and the reflexive one shows one. Which is the kind of definition a formalisation exists to fix, and the reason a finding computed before it is fixed is worth very little. Found by claude-10."}
