           :quote "the `>>>` block-quote convention is\nimplemented in the Emacs path alone."}
  :column :pattern
  :author "claude-1"
  :status :draft
  :refs ["futon3c/emacs/session-turn-analysis.el" "futon3c/scripts/turn_batch.py"]
  :body "Rob's proposed DOCUMENT exit criterion, and the measurement that makes it a seam rather than a tidy-up. The >>> fence is implemented in session-turn-analysis.el and nowhere else: grep finds it in one file, and turn_batch.py carries no quotes[] at all. So a turn recorded live has its quoted block replaced by QUOTE with the text kept beside the record, and the same turn recorded through the batch path keeps the block inline as though Joe had said it. Two writers of one format, disagreeing about what the format means. The sentence splitters were checked against each other on abbreviations, decimals and URLs and agree, so the drift is in what each path knows about the format rather than in how either parses a sentence \u2014 which is the kind of divergence a declared interface would have prevented and a convention did not."}
